# Project Instructions — <REPO> (lite mode, v2.0)

This claude.ai Project uses **lite mode** of claude_researcher
(`github.com/danparshall/claude_researcher`, `template_lite/`), an
open-source workflow I chose for small utility repos that don't need the
full research machinery: each session reads where things stand from my repo
and commits its progress back.

**One repo per Project, by default.** This Project's repo is
`<USERNAME>/<REPO>`. Every session also reads my config repo,
`<USERNAME>/claude_research_config`, which holds `personal_info.md`: the
profile I wrote so you know who I am, how I work, and which name and email
go on commits. When the work needs another of my repos, you can attach it:
when I name it, or after asking me.

```bash
PI_VERSION="2.0"
USER=<USERNAME>
REPO=<REPO>
USER_DISPLAY_NAME="<USER_DISPLAY_NAME>"
COMMIT_EMAIL="<COMMIT_EMAIL>"
GIT_FLUENCY="<GIT_FLUENCY>"
```

The last three are copies of fields in `personal_info.md`, here so a
session can start even if reading that file is refused.

## Session start

1. Attach `${USER}/${REPO}` and `${USER}/claude_research_config` read-only
   with the add-repository tool (`add_repo`; if it isn't listed, load it with the
   tool search query `select:mcp__claude-code-remote__add_repo`), one call each, same turn.
2. Clone the repo, then read `LITE.md` at its root. That file is the runtime
   spec (memory model, disposition, session-end rules) and takes precedence
   over anything here except the values above:

   ```bash
   git clone --depth 1 "https://github.com/${USER}/${REPO}.git" /home/claude/${REPO}
   ```

3. Read `personal_info.md` with `curl`, not WebFetch (the repo is private;
   the sandbox's GitHub proxy authenticates, so send no token):

   ```bash
   curl -s -H "Accept: application/vnd.github+json" \
     -H "X-GitHub-Api-Version: 2022-11-28" \
     "https://api.github.com/repos/$USER/claude_research_config/contents/personal_info.md" \
     | python3 -c "import sys,json,base64; print(base64.b64decode(json.load(sys.stdin)['content']).decode())"
   ```

   Read `Git fluency`, `Interaction style`, `Home repo`, `Tools and
   languages`, and any preferences relevant to the session. If the read
   fails or is refused, tell me once with the exact error and carry on with
   the copies above; don't retry it.

At the first commit, request push for `${USER}/${REPO}` with the
add-repository tool, then push (`LITE.md` has the details).

The record is `STATUS.md`, `DECISIONS.md` and `git log`, not past chats;
skip `conversation_search` / `recent_chats` at session start. If anything
here looks inconsistent with my setup (wrong username, wrong repo, missing
values), stop and say so before doing any work.
